---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { ENTITY } from "../data/legal";

const UPDATED = "2026-10-12";
---

<LegalLayout
	title="Cookie Notice"
	description="Which cookies and similar storage this MedicSupport Network website uses — and which it does not."
	updated={UPDATED}
>
	<h2>The short version</h2>
	<p>
		<strong>This website does not set any cookies.</strong> It runs no analytics, no
		advertising technology, no social-media trackers, no fingerprinting, and no
		third-party marketing scripts. There is no cookie banner on this site because there is
		nothing to consent to.
	</p>

	<h2>Why there is no banner</h2>
	<p>
		A consent banner exists to let visitors refuse tracking that requires consent. Since we
		collect no such data, adding a banner would be misleading: it would imply we track
		people when we do not. We will add one, and change this page, if that ever ceases to be
		true.
	</p>

	<h2>What we do not do</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>No analytics packages (no Google Analytics, Plausible, Matomo, Fathom or similar).</li>
		<li>No advertising, retargeting or conversion pixels.</li>
		<li>No social media embeds or share widgets that would phone home when you read a page.</li>
		<li>No consent-management platform writing to <code>localStorage</code>.</li>
		<li>No canvas, audio or font-based fingerprinting.</li>
		<li>No cross-site or cross-page tracking of your reading.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>What is stored on your device</h2>
	<p>Nothing. This site does not write to <code>localStorage</code>, <code>sessionStorage</code>,
		IndexedDB, or the Cache API for its own purposes.</p>

	<h2>Server logs</h2>
	<p>
		Like any web server, the platform that hosts this site records request logs — IP address,
		timestamp, requested URL, user agent, response status — in order to serve the site,
		detect abuse, and diagnose faults. These are <strong>server logs, not cookies</strong>,
		and they are not used to build a profile of you or to follow you elsewhere. They are
		handled in line with our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Embedded content and third parties</h2>
	<p>
		Where a page embeds or links to another organisation's service — for example a
		professional register — that organisation's own privacy terms apply once you follow the
		link. We do not embed third-party content that would track you without your action.
	</p>

	<h2>Fonts</h2>
	<p>
		Typography is served from our own asset host. No request is made to a font provider that
		would reveal your visit to them.
	</p>

	<h2>If this changes</h2>
	<p>
		If we introduce cookies or similar storage that requires consent, this page will be
		updated first, and a consent banner will appear before any such technology is set. Until
		then, this page is the accurate description of what the site does.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Questions about this notice: <a href={`mailto:${ENTITY.generalEmail}`}
			>{ENTITY.generalEmail}</a
		>.
	</p>
</LegalLayout>